              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "**[wakehealth.edu](https://www.wakehealth.edu/)** is the official website for **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist** (formerly known as Wake Forest Baptist Health). Based in Winston-Salem, North Carolina, it is a nationally recognized academic medical center and healthcare system associated with the Wake Forest University School of Medicine and Charlotte-based Advocate Health.\n\nWhether you are a patient, student, job seeker, or medical professional, the website serves as the primary gateway to their services. \n\n---\n\n### 1. Patient Services & Portals\n* **MyAtriumHealth (Patient Portal):** The old **myWakeHealth** patient portal has transitioned to **MyAtriumHealth** (powered by Epic MyChart). You can log in using your existing myWakeHealth credentials.\n  * **What you can do:** View test results, message your healthcare provider, request prescription refills, schedule appointments, and manage medical bills.\n  * **Login link:** [MyAtriumHealth Patient Portal](https://my.atriumhealth.org/)\n* **Find a Doctor:** Search for primary care doctors, pediatricians, or specialists across the network.\n* **Locations:** Find directions and contact information for major hospitals (like Brenner Children\u2019s Hospital, Davie Medical Center, High Point Medical Center, Lexington Medical Center, and Wilkes Medical Center), as well as local urgent care and primary care clinics.\n* **Billing & Payments:** For medical services received on or after March 2, 2024, bills can be paid directly through your MyAtriumHealth account. For older outstanding bills, you will find instructions for pay-by-mail or phone options on the main website.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Education & Research\nBecause Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist is an academic medical center, `wakehealth.edu` hosts extensive resources for students and researchers through the **Wake Forest University School of Medicine**:\n* **Academic Programs:** Information on MD programs, physician assistant (PA) programs, nurse anesthesia (CRNA), and biomedical graduate degrees.\n* **Residencies and Fellowships:** Portals for medical school graduates seeking training.\n* **Clinical Trials:** A database of active medical research studies and clinical trials open for public enrollment.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Employee & Career Resources\n* **Careers:** Search and apply for open job listings, nursing positions, and physician opportunities.\n* **Employee Portals:** Dedicated access links for active staff members (requiring internal login credentials) to check work email, use the PeopleSoft system, or log into training portals.\n\n---\n\n### Looking for Immediate Help?\n* **Main Appointment Line:** 888-716-9253 (Toll-Free)\n* **MyAtriumHealth Technical Support:** 855-799-0044\n* **General Emergencies:** Please call **911** if you are experiencing a medical emergency.",
